## Part B — Local dev environment (reproducible)

Autonomy requires a one-command-up environment so the agent can run and verify.

- **One-command-up local environment** appropriate to `{{STACK}}` (e.g. `docker compose up -d` for containerized dependencies, or the equivalent for the chosen stack). The goal: DB, queue, and any required services start without cloud round-trips.
- **`.env.example`** documenting every required variable: connection strings, API keys, service credentials, etc. Never commit real values.
- **Scripts** in the package manifest: `dev`, `build`, `test`, `test:e2e`, `lint`, and any DB/migration commands.
- **Seed/fixtures** for a demo project so flows are runnable end-to-end without manual data entry.

Document the exact commands in `CLAUDE.md` "Commands" once they exist — the agent reads them to self-serve.

