## Part D — What the agent needs from you to work autonomously

Provide these and the agent can run long stretches unsupervised. Until then, work is gated.

**Decisions to close:**
- [ ] Package manager (decided: **{{PACKAGE_MANAGER}}**).
- [ ] Operating approach for code-writing agents: write directly to repos, or generate patches for review first? (Recommend: patches/review first.)
- [ ] Any integration-specific choices for the project (payment, voice, doc export, etc.) — document decisions in `docs/develop/DECISIONS.md`.

**Access & secrets (via `.env`, never committed):**
- [ ] External service credentials (DB, auth, storage, AI APIs) — see `.env.example` for required variables.
- [ ] Queue/cache instance (or use local docker-compose equivalent).
- [ ] For the Local Runner: which local repos map to which projects.

**Operating contract:**
- [ ] Confirm: commit/push only when you ask.
- [ ] Confirm: scope authority = source docs MVP; anything outside needs your OK.
- [ ] Confirm: approval gates for the high-risk actions in C9.
- [ ] Per-task acceptance criteria (or authorize the agent to draft them and proceed).

**Already provided / not blocking:** the source docs, framework decision, this conditioning plan.

